    {"id":"continuum:population:definition-v1","game":"continuum","subjectId":"population","text":"The World Bank counts residents regardless of citizenship or legal status; its population totals are midyear estimates.","sourceUrl":"https://databank.worldbank.org/metadataglossary/world-development-indicators/series/SP.POP.TOTL","sourceTitle":"World Bank: Population, total","sourceSection":"Long definition","reviewedAt":"2026-09-26","contentFingerprint":"1055006deaa9b5ccd1ba2a14af5eaf6d66c7641d4347a6eacfef81b9959711c1"},
    {"id":"continuum:area:definition-v1","game":"continuum","subjectId":"area","text":"Country surface area includes inland water and some coastal waterways, so it is different from land area alone.","sourceUrl":"https://databank.worldbank.org/metadataglossary/world-development-indicators/series/AG.SRF.TOTL.K2","sourceTitle":"World Bank: Surface area","sourceSection":"Long definition","reviewedAt":"2026-09-26","contentFingerprint":"8a9dbee531777ea94cca428777b4e37a146613a32e9254a787524d63b9f2c3ba"},
    {"id":"continuum:gdp_per_capita:definition-v1","game":"continuum","subjectId":"gdp_per_capita","text":"GDP per capita divides economic output by population. A current-US-dollar figure is not adjusted for price changes over time.","sourceUrl":"https://data360files.worldbank.org/data360-data/metadata/WB_WDI/WB_WDI_NY_GDP_PCAP_CD.pdf","sourceTitle":"World Bank: GDP per capita (current US$), metadata v1.1.1","sourceSection":"Definition, PDF page 3","reviewedAt":"2026-09-26","contentFingerprint":"c7160d862cd8e4046b323938de5f089cbddb4833e7ae75f51bde11ec5840d2c4"},
    {"id":"continuum:AtomicNumber:definition-v1","game":"continuum","subjectId":"AtomicNumber","text":"An element’s atomic number counts the protons in its nucleus.","sourceUrl":"https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/A00499","sourceTitle":"IUPAC Gold Book: atomic number","sourceSection":"Definition","reviewedAt":"2026-09-26","contentFingerprint":"7885b7bf3590195c55470f5be16bda4a9be2ccb4c57316f621b3cdb9e96a9e6a"},
    {"id":"continuum:Density:definition-v1","game":"continuum","subjectId":"Density","text":"Density measures mass in a given volume. The Royal Society of Chemistry lists element densities at room temperature.","sourceUrl":"https://periodic-table.rsc.org/element/26/iron","sourceTitle":"Royal Society of Chemistry: element glossary","sourceSection":"Density glossary","reviewedAt":"2026-09-26","contentFingerprint":"70998954055848ad2e4d46904be0454f5f8afae1b74042a1cd6fd6b515125859"},
    {"id":"continuum:AtomicRadius:definition-v1","game":"continuum","subjectId":"AtomicRadius","text":"Atomic radius depends on the definition: covalent radii describe bonded atoms, while non-bonded radii use atoms that are not bonded.","sourceUrl":"https://periodic-table.rsc.org/element/26/iron","sourceTitle":"Royal Society of Chemistry: element glossary","sourceSection":"Atomic radius, non-bonded; Covalent radius","reviewedAt":"2026-09-26","contentFingerprint":"f588c42e5a582c741047895490ec7b9feb033f91afbe45a912dbae8998d9cc71"}
